{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_030 (multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.678 accuracy, a large jump over config_026 (singleprofile, same encoders/fusion) at 0.540, confirming multiprofile aggregation is the dominant design lever. The remaining uncertainty is whether the simple avgpool aggregation is sufficient or whether a transformer-based aggregation over profiles can capture richer inter-profile interactions. Question tested: config_020 keeps the exact same encoders (scvi_n200, resnet50) and fusion (weighted) as config_030 but replaces avgpool with transformer aggregation, isolating the aggregation method as the single variable. Why this is the best next experiment: it is the most direct and informative extension of our best result, targeting the component most likely to yield further accuracy gains (profile-to-profile relationship modeling). The expected cost is moderate—roughly 7–8 GPU hours (slightly above config_030's 5.90 due to attention over profiles, but no heavier image encoder), keeping total spend around ~14 GPU hours and leaving ample budget for 6 follow-up experiments to explore image-encoder upgrades or fusion changes if transformer aggregation proves beneficial."
}

